= The Spandrels of San Marco and the Panglossian Paradigm: A Critique of the Adaptationist Programme / 圣马可的拱肩与潘格洛斯范式：对适应主义纲领的批评

#html.p(id: "en-G001")[#text("The architectural starting point is memorable: spaces produced by a building's structure can later carry elaborate decoration. Their present appearance alone does not explain why those spaces exist.")]

#zh(id: "G001")[#text("文章的建筑切入点很容易记住：建筑结构产生的空间，后来可以承载精美的装饰。仅凭它们现在的样子，并不能解释这些空间为什么存在。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G002")[#text("Gould and Lewontin use this analogy to question explanations that assign an adaptive purpose to every trait. Development, history, and structural constraints also belong in the account.")]

#zh(id: "G002")[#text("古尔德与莱温廷借此质疑一种解释习惯：为每个性状都安排一个适应用途。发育、历史与结构约束，也应当进入解释。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G003")[#text("The challenge is to compare alternatives and ask what evidence discriminates among them. A convincing story about usefulness is a starting hypothesis, rather than its own confirmation.")]

#zh(id: "G003")[#text("关键是比较不同解释，并问什么证据能够区分它们。一个关于用途的动人故事，可以成为初始假说，却不能自己证明自己。")]

#html.p(id: "en-G004")[#text("Reading question: if the proposed function disappeared, could the feature still arise? Keep this question separate from the broader question of whether natural selection operates.")]

#zh(id: "G004")[#text("阅读时可以追问：如果所提出的功能不存在，这个特征是否仍可能出现？这个问题要与自然选择是否起作用的宏观问题区分开来。")]
